# What the API image must never see.
#
# The builder stage does `COPY . .`, so anything not listed here is uploaded to
# the daemon on every build and then baked into a layer. Before this file
# excluded them, `ai-sidecar/` (879 MB of virtualenv and Piper voices) and
# `hospital-management-system/` (288 MB of an unrelated frontend) made a
# ~1.2 GB context for an image whose useful content is about 8 MB.

node_modules
dist
coverage
*.log

.git
.gitignore
.github
.husky
.vscode
.agents

# Secrets, and the trap. The tracked `.env` points DATABASE_URL at the
# production host; baking it into the image would mean a container that happened
# to start without an explicit DATABASE_URL would fall through to production.
# Compose supplies every variable the container needs.
.env*

# The sidecar is its own image (ai-sidecar/Dockerfile) with its own build
# context, and `.venv` + `voices/` are 879 MB of it.
ai-sidecar

# A separate frontend checked in beside the API. Nothing in the Nest build
# reads it, and tsconfig.json already excludes it from compilation.
hospital-management-system

# Docs and compose files change constantly and would bust the cache layer for
# `COPY . .` on every edit, for content the runtime never opens.
README.md
DEMO.md
api-documentation.md
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
